  "structure": {
    "block_count": 29,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Roots Showing? Expert Tips For Safe Hair Coloring in Pregnancy",
        "text_sha256": "abcdd3a6608827742cba69bea3a047526664f86b6dea311539c3b26b30f1fc5f",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "woman getting her hair colored",
        "text_sha256": "faa000b51f13dabb90d1b3127990144d9fffb9b4e71e4e8f7240ba58d823aa8a",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Being pregnant doesn't mean you can't have fabulous hair — just exercise a little caution and common sense.",
        "text_sha256": "5799502c20f507fa797f3cf47bd2db450be4ef25950a7ef8b17c915a6720a255",
        "word_count": 18
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Swollen ankles, stretch marks , an itchy belly ... some things are inevitable when you're pregnant. But roots and grays? Not necessarily.",
        "text_sha256": "00fa52c79cd32bf380a7db13e8d0ff3b219be33309e90653dc5fdd2e418bef97",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Hair dye is safe — particularly after the first trimester. It's best to wait a bit (until the second trimester), since a few chemicals from hair dye are absorbed by the scalp.",
        "text_sha256": "aba92a9b8566772c0b1a24d2f1c1e4ad499966307f84b95299e1991c813f701c",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Pick gentle techniques. Highlights, lowlights, and streaks are safest as they don't touch skin, along with solutions made without ammonia and plant-based henna dyes.",
        "text_sha256": "05e54a57835a7adba024ab6fa373ae45daa5cc645cdaa9c678d86d4b4f1b3385",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Safety first! Color your locks in a well-ventilated space, wear gloves, and do a test run on a small section of hair to check for any reaction.",
        "text_sha256": "90bdf9a754d3a7670b7bdc5a0849695bd2116a876fd87d655d8d738936a29f1a",
        "word_count": 27
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Can you dye your hair while pregnant?",
        "text_sha256": "23efeeb9db556736a63f6e6c35ad3928b1fb1804232c02330550a1d3ccd86583",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Yes, you can dye your hair while you're pregnant — as long as you take certain precautions and mention your pregnancy to your stylist. Here are five tips to ensure you get the hair color you want while protecting your baby-to-be.",
        "text_sha256": "64112aece5bb31a459ad918246c68bc6ebffaa65e2acc6e56bde026a89e64beb",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Wait until the second trimester",
        "text_sha256": "26c16a7b2d717e425ccbc448063a038b0ec78dd7136352aa3bd8cb72c0550d2f",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Is it safe to use hair dye during pregnancy ? Research on this subject is limited, but many experts advise mothers-to-be to wait until around the beginning of the second trimester .",
        "text_sha256": "158c76358567b647e64650c0f2c40d894bd78e00e0d4105781474d4b8f531f76",
        "word_count": 32
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "No doubt, you may be ready to hit the bottle (of hair dye, that is) after about a month. With all of those pregnancy hormones racing through your body, your hair may be growing faster than ever and may even have a different texture and color than you're used to.",
        "text_sha256": "819da9639e0d6f8d71d1f46c89b4dec7f5a2a556d42c00f0d92c355b19f37ee4",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "But the first 13 weeks are a time of major development for your baby: Organs are taking shape, muscles and vocal chords are forming, and nail beds and hair follicles are starting to develop. Even though you don't absorb much of the chemicals in hair dye — and there's actually no hard evidence that those chemicals are indeed harmful to your baby — why take the chance?",
        "text_sha256": "c61a07f91d91a64915a864673762a4e80ee5c575b15dcbd888373165ff073b34",
        "word_count": 67
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Opt for the safest services",
        "text_sha256": "7adfeb743cb3a54776b477b3e619433d929622fde03987022a9c2773426ad3d9",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Once you get the go-ahead from your doctor to book the salon appointment, you may want to reconsider which service you get. Root touch-ups and a root-to-tip color change are considered single-process color; this means dye is applied to the hair and scalp, where the pores in your skin soak up the chemicals, which can enter your bloodstream.",
        "text_sha256": "71cf7b048660322ab4f576acae576e77bf00f96aaa518fb6ec0e490bd88dbed4",
        "word_count": 58
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "For a safer alternative, try techniques where color is painted directly on to the hair shaft — highlights, lowlights, frosting, and streaking, for example. Pulling hair through a cap and then applying color is a less common method but equally as safe, since the cap covers the scalp.",
        "text_sha256": "a2af7a8971c04348083d24c223f331ad039c6e46ed10602d60fa803cf8c60313",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Get the answer to every beauty question under the sun with the What to Expect app , your trusted resource when it comes to pregnancy hair, nails, skin, and more.",
        "text_sha256": "f555595d358485fff13b9a07d847c604289ca25cc29829f04a568bc6ed4461fa",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Use gentle color",
        "text_sha256": "f488de5d199461b364e1c433a7dc8edb8432a1671c7991630b53301a8f9b7121",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Also important to keep in mind is the type of coloring you use. Ask your stylist about gentler options, like color with an ammonia-free base.",
        "text_sha256": "04be5a71cea121c6e270dc5e5dc46909009d7f91de0eee10bdddd9f8f8671bcc",
        "word_count": 25
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're more of the DIY type, consider a semi-permanent color — it doesn't contain ammonia and typically doesn't contain peroxide (bleach). Plus, it's more forgiving than permanent dyes, and fades gradually after a month or so.",
        "text_sha256": "65b14a8533cb8098813bf2159074e0f80d31e45a3f4999531705596faf8be509",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Vegetable and henna dyes are other less-toxic at-home alternatives, though check the label before buying. Some so-called \"natural\" processes contain just as many chemicals as their traditional counterparts.",
        "text_sha256": "0e5961f2c700320efdf6deb36c42ffb4f9ba7bb189fa552f6fc98b8102f28432",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hair questions abound among What to Expect Community parents. One parent, madiminx, spoke with her doctor about hair dye and was told to use \"a less harsh dye, like a semi-permanent one, and to keep it off my scalp.\"",
        "text_sha256": "98841f4f98560587ec317ee91e9282292124d5631b3f07a75e4af0e225fee40b",
        "word_count": 39
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Keep ventilated and covered",
        "text_sha256": "4350e0a6cc04c360153926eac60834840bb0504c89b206a71fda28338204722d",
        "word_count": 4
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "When it comes time to start coloring, experts agree you should take some extra safety precautions. If you're in a salon, ask to be seated in a well-ventilated area.",
        "text_sha256": "1a231072f175aaa5cd88f38e9e3f31cf60fb8dc98420fbda0e9835d6171ffe4c",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you're at home, open up the windows so you're breathing in fresh air, not toxic fumes. Always wear gloves if you're applying the product to your own hair, and slip into a long-sleeved shirt for extra coverage. Follow the manufacturer's directions, leave the dye on for the minimum time recommended, and be sure to wash your scalp thoroughly when the job is done.",
        "text_sha256": "5b01129cceb5913efab568c66b92d2aa3b21b3e324d52f3b52bce43fbe36e4f1",
        "word_count": 64
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "If possible, test a strand first",
        "text_sha256": "1abb588f56ef2e9f59330d1fa3679fe4339edb7fb5185a663bc5c063f28eef9d",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Remember that hormonal changes can make your hair react differently, so you might not get what you expect — even from your regular formula. Before you do your whole head, try a test strand so you don't wind up punk pink — unless that's the look you were going for, of course!",
        "text_sha256": "642b24412af7c1c1f59ee4f39121fd7c1615d1c372ba59b9be494649db4feb1a",
        "word_count": 52
      }
    ],
    "content_word_count": 776,
    "heading_count": 8
  },
  "title": "Roots Showing? Expert Tips For Safe Hair Coloring in Pregnancy",
